# SupraLINUX NetworkManagerQt packaging

KDE Frameworks 6.30.0 is the source/build authority. Ubuntu Resolute and Debian sid
packaging trees are compatibility references only.

The full symbols file is intentionally not duplicated in Git. The Batch 5 hosted
runner verifies and injects the exact Debian 6.28.0 baseline from workflow run
34708030450 / artifact 10301938362 before dpkg-source -b. Debian is selected for
the symbols baseline because it is closer to KDE 6.30; Ubuntu remains the direct
binary-compatibility target. Any KDE 6.30 ABI delta must be reviewed from a real build.

Symbols reference: `libkf6networkmanagerqt6.symbols`, SHA-256 `324a154e35a6dab6c2ab10c5857517a20253d7d65f279294a62e7ced3c8ebfaa`.
Copyright reference SHA-256: `c6d6d851fc0ac1e99ab9d5535159213b3ba4a7deff6a4239f76e59fb51316e1e`.

QDoc is disabled in the current common Frameworks profile. The established
documentation binary package name is retained as a compatibility stub and does not
claim QCH payload. Upstream autotests remain enabled except for explicitly documented
service-dependent tests that cannot be satisfied in the isolated package-build lane.

NetworkManagerQt upstream tests `managertest`, `settingstest` and `activeconnectiontest` require a live NetworkManager service. The isolated sbuild lane excludes only those three tests; all other upstream tests remain enabled.
